{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1446719-adventure-where-did-my-cliffhanger-rules-go","id":1446719,"title":"Adventure! - where did my cliffhanger rules go?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-30T19:46:13-07:00","id":1446719,"title":"Adventure! - where did my cliffhanger rules go?","content":"While I imagine I could fairly easily hack some together from the basic Dramatic Editing rules, I have to admit I was really bummed to see that the 1e cliffhanger subsystem didn't come back in the new edition. Is there any chance they might return in a future supplement or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24779-shisumo","name":"Shisumo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T23:03:14-07:00","id":1446746,"title":"","content":"Technically, a cliffhanger was never a rule; it was a storytelling technique: put the party in terrible jeopardy at the end of the game session, then let them spend their time until the next session dreaming up ways to use Dramatic Editing to get out of their predicament. What rules are needed that aren't already there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T12:43:09-07:00","id":1448454,"title":"","content":"They weren't huge, but there were specific mechanics for cliffhangers in Adventure! 1E. Three, to be precise: NPCs cannot spend Inspiration during cliffhangers, there is a specific order in which Inspiration is spent, starting with the lowest base Initiative and working up, and PCs have exactly one action, with or without Dramatic Editing, they get to take before the Storyteller resolves the cliffhanger. None of those things are true with ordinary Dramatic Editing.<br /> <br /> The specific mechanics are mostly beside the point, however. For me, at least, it's more about addressing the genre expectation and providing a Storyguide with suggestions and guidelines for incorporating cliffhangers into their games - the same basic topics that comprised the majority of the 1E cliffhanger section, in other words. The utter absence of the very <i>word</i> &quot;cliffhanger&quot; in the manuscript of a game about pulp action/adventure strikes me as missing a pretty fundamental element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24779-shisumo","name":"Shisumo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}